"╻  ╻┏━╸╺┳╸┏━┓┏━╸┏━╸
┃  ┃┣╸  ┃ ┃ ┃┣╸ ┣╸
┗━╸╹╹   ╹ ┗━┛╹  ╹
Mission Control Liftoff 0.12.3 - Initialize a governed application and prepare
its local workstation.
Usage
─────
liftoff <command> [options]

Global options
──────────────
Option     Description
─────────  ──────────────────────────────────
--version  Show the installed Liftoff version
--help     Show general help

Onboarding
──────────
Command  Description
───────  ────────────────────────────────────────────────
init     Initialize a project and prepare its workstation
plan     Preview generated artifacts
migrate  Adopt an existing project

Maintenance
───────────
Command   Description
────────  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
assess    Read-only whole-project comparison against explicitly displayed
          installed targets
adopt     Preview reviewed in-place adoption for a supported non-Liftoff
          application
workflow  Review an explicit development-workflow transition
validate  Validate a generated project manifest
update    Preview and explicitly approve scoped project updates
repair    Review and repair supported project files with separate default-No
          approval
upgrade   Replace the supported global npm Liftoff CLI; project templates use
          update separately
doctor    Check local and project readiness

Reference
─────────
Command       Description
────────────  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
help          Show general or command-specific help
patterns      List GenAI patterns
capabilities  Inspect installed public capabilities without project or readiness
              probes
providers     List cloud providers
regions       List or search provider regions

Operations
──────────
Command     Description
──────────  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
governance  Plan, approve, execute, recover, and inspect scoped governance work
dev         Print Docker Compose helper commands
infra       Print OpenTofu helper commands

i Tip: Run \`liftoff help <command>\` for command-specific usage.
"
`;

exports[`complete help screens > snapshots compact governance assessment help 1`] = `
"LIFTOFF / GOVERNANCE ASSESS
Read-only comparison against the installed CLI policy, activation identity, and
control catalog. Local-only by default: no network or credentials required. Exit
0: aligned or explicitly disabled (not-applicable); 2: partial coverage or
differences, including approved exceptions; 1: invalid or unsafe input. This is
not setup, an upgrade, or permission to remediate.

Usage
─────
liftoff governance assess [project-path] [--json] [--live]

Arguments
─────────
Argument      Description
────────────  ──────────────────────────
project-path  Liftoff project to inspect

Project options
───────────────
Option            Description
────────────────  ────────────────────
--project <path>  Liftoff project path

Consent options
───────────────
Option  Description
──────  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--live  Opt into bounded repository/resource-scoped GitHub/Azure reads using
        existing permissions; denied or unavailable proof stays not-observed

Output options
──────────────
Option  Description
──────  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--json  Emit the schema-v1 report with pinned target, findings, provenance, and
        coverage to stdout; never write state or evidence

General options
───────────────
Option  Description
──────  ──────────────────────────
--help  Show command-specific help

"
`;

exports[`complete help screens > snapshots compact governance command help 1`] = `
"LIFTOFF / GOVERNANCE
Historical projects retain schema-2 planning and execution. V8 projects retain
schema-3 status, resume and verify inspection; recorded phases are not current
proof. An exact --revalidation-publication selects existing successor proof,
never approval or execution. Verify exits 0 for complete or inapplicable
selected scope, 2 for consistent incomplete work, and 1 for inspection failure.
For separate schema-7 v8 verification, select --scope local --local-operation
verify: plan --inputs <request.json>, approve --plan <fingerprint> --inputs
<consent.json>, then apply-next --plan <fingerprint> --execute. Planning probes
installed tools and saves an external preview; approval separately saves
consent. Without --execute, apply-next only inspects saved progress. Keep public
request and consent files outside the project. Native Manual uses
verify-manual-native and approve-manual-native with independent infrastructure
preparation/network consent and the advertised qualified host/tool limits.
Locked provider downloads and local validation grant no Azure/GitHub resource
operations. Initialized OpenSpec requires explicit generated-baseline scope
attestation; it is not domain verification; the private workspace is not a
sandbox. Separate schema-5 completion uses --local-operation finalize for
admitted Manual/Spec Kit verification, then --local-operation publish for exact
target review, independent approval and execution. Both require their own closed
--inputs for plan/approve and exact --plan for apply-next. For publication,
governance recover --plan <fingerprint> --execute recovers only that attributed
transaction; without --execute it only inspects saved progress. Failure does not
imply rollback. Separate schema-6 --local-operation revalidate-successor
constructs or reviews exact records from completed verification of an existing
supported successor; it requires independent publication approval and explicit
execution/recovery. Committed incomplete revalidation stays active and exits 2.
No successor creation, OpenSpec finalization, provider or whole-directory
rollback authority is granted. Local operations otherwise exit 0 for a completed
requested operation or nonexecuting inspection, and 1 for refusal, failure, or
uncertainty.

Usage
─────
liftoff governance
<status|plan|approve|apply-next|credential-enroll|recover|resume|verify|assess>
[project-path]

Arguments
─────────
Argument      Description
────────────  ──────────────────────────
project-path  Liftoff project to inspect

Subcommands
───────────
- status
- plan
- approve
- apply-next
- credential-enroll
- recover
- resume
- verify
- assess

Project options
───────────────
Option            Description
────────────────  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--project <path>  Liftoff project path
--inputs <file>   Public activation configuration or explicit local
                  request/consent JSON; never credentials or state

Command options
───────────────
Option                                   Description
───────────────────────────────────────  ───────────────────────────────────────
--scope <scope>                          Execution/verification boundary: local,
                                         activation, or lifecycle (default:
                                         activation)
--local-operation <operation>            v8 only: verify, finalize, publish, or
                                         revalidate-successor with --scope
                                         local; publication operations also
                                         support recover
--revalidation-publication               Inspect one exact v8 successor
<fingerprint>                            publication; not approval or execution
--recover-phase <phase>                  Plan explicit recovery of one failed or
                                         interrupted phase without executing it

Consent options
───────────────
Option                Description
────────────────────  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--plan <fingerprint>  Exact project-bound fingerprint from governance plan
--protected-stdin     Credential enrollment is currently unavailable; this flag
                      reads no secret
--execute             Execute the reviewed apply-next/recover operation;
                      planning and approval save external metadata separately
--live                Assess only: request bounded read-only GitHub/Azure
                      metadata with existing permissions

Output options
──────────────
Option  Description
──────  ──────────────────────────
--json  Emit machine-readable JSON

General options
───────────────
Option  Description
──────  ──────────────────────────
--help  Show command-specific help

"
`;

