exports[`complete help screens > snapshots plain general help 1`] = `
"Liftoff - Mission Control Liftoff 0.12.3 - Initialize a governed application and prepare its local workstation.

Usage
liftoff <command> [options]

Global options
Option: --version | Description: Show the installed Liftoff version
Option: --help | Description: Show general help

Onboarding
Command: init | Description: Initialize a project and prepare its workstation
Command: plan | Description: Preview generated artifacts
Command: migrate | Description: Adopt an existing project

Maintenance
Command: assess | Description: Read-only whole-project comparison against explicitly displayed installed targets
Command: adopt | Description: Preview reviewed in-place adoption for a supported non-Liftoff application
Command: workflow | Description: Review an explicit development-workflow transition
Command: validate | Description: Validate a generated project manifest
Command: update | Description: Preview and explicitly approve scoped project updates
Command: repair | Description: Review and repair supported project files with separate default-No approval
Command: upgrade | Description: Replace the supported global npm Liftoff CLI; project templates use update separately
Command: doctor | Description: Check local and project readiness

Reference
Command: help | Description: Show general or command-specific help
Command: patterns | Description: List GenAI patterns
Command: capabilities | Description: Inspect installed public capabilities without project or readiness probes
Command: providers | Description: List cloud providers
Command: regions | Description: List or search provider regions

Operations
Command: governance | Description: Plan, approve, execute, recover, and inspect scoped governance work
Command: dev | Description: Print Docker Compose helper commands
Command: infra | Description: Print OpenTofu helper commands

[info] Tip: Run \`liftoff help <command>\` for command-specific usage.
"
`;

exports[`complete help screens > snapshots plain governance assessment help 1`] = `
"LIFTOFF / GOVERNANCE ASSESS - Read-only comparison against the installed CLI policy, activation identity, and control catalog. Local-only by default: no network or credentials required. Exit 0: aligned or explicitly disabled (not-applicable); 2: partial coverage or differences, including approved exceptions; 1: invalid or unsafe input. This is not setup, an upgrade, or permission to remediate.

Usage
Usage: liftoff governance assess [project-path] [--json] [--live]

Arguments
Argument: project-path | Description: Liftoff project to inspect

Project options
Option: --project <path> | Description: Liftoff project path

Consent options
Option: --live | Description: Opt into bounded repository/resource-scoped GitHub/Azure reads using existing permissions; denied or unavailable proof stays not-observed

Output options
Option: --json | Description: Emit the schema-v1 report with pinned target, findings, provenance, and coverage to stdout; never write state or evidence

General options
Option: --help | Description: Show command-specific help

"
`;

exports[`complete help screens > snapshots plain governance command help 1`] = `
"LIFTOFF / GOVERNANCE - Historical projects retain schema-2 planning and execution. V8 projects retain schema-3 status, resume and verify inspection; recorded phases are not current proof. An exact --revalidation-publication selects existing successor proof, never approval or execution. Verify exits 0 for complete or inapplicable selected scope, 2 for consistent incomplete work, and 1 for inspection failure. For separate schema-7 v8 verification, select --scope local --local-operation verify: plan --inputs <request.json>, approve --plan <fingerprint> --inputs <consent.json>, then apply-next --plan <fingerprint> --execute. Planning probes installed tools and saves an external preview; approval separately saves consent. Without --execute, apply-next only inspects saved progress. Keep public request and consent files outside the project. Native Manual uses verify-manual-native and approve-manual-native with independent infrastructure preparation/network consent and the advertised qualified host/tool limits. Locked provider downloads and local validation grant no Azure/GitHub resource operations. Initialized OpenSpec requires explicit generated-baseline scope attestation; it is not domain verification; the private workspace is not a sandbox. Separate schema-5 completion uses --local-operation finalize for admitted Manual/Spec Kit verification, then --local-operation publish for exact target review, independent approval and execution. Both require their own closed --inputs for plan/approve and exact --plan for apply-next. For publication, governance recover --plan <fingerprint> --execute recovers only that attributed transaction; without --execute it only inspects saved progress. Failure does not imply rollback. Separate schema-6 --local-operation revalidate-successor constructs or reviews exact records from completed verification of an existing supported successor; it requires independent publication approval and explicit execution/recovery. Committed incomplete revalidation stays active and exits 2. No successor creation, OpenSpec finalization, provider or whole-directory rollback authority is granted. Local operations otherwise exit 0 for a completed requested operation or nonexecuting inspection, and 1 for refusal, failure, or uncertainty.

Usage
Usage: liftoff governance <status|plan|approve|apply-next|credential-enroll|recover|resume|verify|assess> [project-path]

Arguments
Argument: project-path | Description: Liftoff project to inspect

Subcommands
- status
- plan
- approve
- apply-next
- credential-enroll
- recover
- resume
- verify
- assess

Project options
Option: --project <path> | Description: Liftoff project path
Option: --inputs <file> | Description: Public activation configuration or explicit local request/consent JSON; never credentials or state

Command options
Option: --scope <scope> | Description: Execution/verification boundary: local, activation, or lifecycle (default: activation)
Option: --local-operation <operation> | Description: v8 only: verify, finalize, publish, or revalidate-successor with --scope local; publication operations also support recover
Option: --revalidation-publication <fingerprint> | Description: Inspect one exact v8 successor publication; not approval or execution
Option: --recover-phase <phase> | Description: Plan explicit recovery of one failed or interrupted phase without executing it

Consent options
Option: --plan <fingerprint> | Description: Exact project-bound fingerprint from governance plan
Option: --protected-stdin | Description: Credential enrollment is currently unavailable; this flag reads no secret
Option: --execute | Description: Execute the reviewed apply-next/recover operation; planning and approval save external metadata separately
Option: --live | Description: Assess only: request bounded read-only GitHub/Azure metadata with existing permissions

Output options
Option: --json | Description: Emit machine-readable JSON

General options
Option: --help | Description: Show command-specific help

"
`;

