exports[`complete help screens > snapshots plain repair command help 1`] = `
"LIFTOFF / REPAIR - Reviewed project repair with independent infrastructure, application and additive-agent scopes. Use --agents to add selections without removing existing agents; --default-agent explicitly changes only a current Spec Kit default. Manual writes only requested Liftoff-native integrations. OpenSpec and Spec Kit use pinned official operations in isolated staging, preserve existing framework history/defaults unless explicitly changed, and reject unknown output or occupied differing destinations. --check and JSON preview without project writes. Workstation tools, the OpenSpec global profile and exact project files require separate permissions. --approve-plan applies one current saved plan; --recover --approve-plan addresses only its authenticated additive-agent transaction. Agent repair remains independently eligible while unrelated application or infrastructure work is incomplete and never claims broader readiness.

Usage
Usage: liftoff repair [project-path]

Arguments
Argument: project-path | Description: Existing Liftoff project; never an initialization destination

Project options
Option: --project <path> | Description: Exact Liftoff project path
Option: --application-patch <patch.json> | Description: Review an exact application patch authored in external staging, not a starter replacement
Option: --subscription <id> | Description: Exact Azure subscription ID for live absence checks

Framework options
Option: --agents <list> | Description: Comma-separated agents to add without removing existing selections; none is invalid (default: codex)
Option: --default-agent <agent> | Description: Explicit new Spec Kit default; the agent is also added when absent

Command options
Option: --check | Description: Preview only; explicit dependency preparation previews include bounded installed-tool identity probes, never project scripts or installs
Option: --capabilities | Description: List repair contracts, recipes, preparation support, schemas and modes without a project or tool probes
Option: --inspect-layout | Description: Inventory actual application paths and current targets without scripts or writes
Option: --recover | Description: Recover only eligible recorded repair effects; additive-agent recovery also requires its exact --approve-plan fingerprint

Consent options
Option: --live | Description: Allow bounded Azure metadata reads with existing authentication; never read state
Option: --approve-plan <fingerprint> | Description: Optional automation: approve one exact saved application, binding, infrastructure, or additive-agent plan; ordinary TTY repair asks instead
Option: --verify-plan <fingerprint> | Description: Optional automation: run exact staged checks; declared preparation/network require separate permissions, never file commit
Option: --allow-dependency-preparation | Description: Separately permit only declared locked private preparation with --verify-plan; not global tools or file writes
Option: --allow-network | Description: Additionally authorize declared network effects for exact --verify-plan checks
Option: --install-tools | Description: Separately authorize pinned framework-tool preparation for an additive agent request
Option: --configure-openspec-profile | Description: Separately authorize the required global OpenSpec profile for an additive OpenSpec agent request

Output options
Option: --json | Description: Emit one schema-2 result (capabilities schema 1); never prompt or implicitly execute

General options
Option: --help | Description: Show command-specific help

Repair approval and native help
- Ordinary liftoff repair displays exact proposed effects, then asks Yes/No with default No on genuine interactive terminals. No fingerprint entry is needed.
- --check only previews. Bare JSON/non-TTY repair never prompts or executes. Exact execution flags are optional automation interfaces; --yes and --force cannot authorize repair.
- Application patches separately request consent for exact project checks, locked private dependency preparation, declared network effects, and file commit. Lifecycle hooks stay suppressed; unsupported enabling blocks. Staging is not an OS or network sandbox.
- Preparation uses existing compatible tools and exact candidate locks, never global installation/configuration or live dependency trees. Only explicit preparation previews probe installed tool identities; capabilities and layout inventory do not.
- Recovery cleans only authenticated CLI-created disposable workspace identities with safely established ownership; never patch staging, live projects, global caches or original-byte backups. Earlier approved effects remain visible after later cancellation.
- Open the selected project in Copilot or Claude and invoke /liftoff-repair; in Codex use $liftoff-repair or its skill picker. These are coding-agent integrations, not shell commands.
- If the native integration is missing, run liftoff update --check for that project and review its separate managed update. See docs/cli-reference.md#repair-modes.

"
`;

exports[`complete help screens > snapshots plain update command help 1`] = `
"LIFTOFF / UPDATE - Start with \`liftoff update --check\`, then run \`liftoff update\` to approve the matching effective plan (default: no). Check leaves project bytes unchanged and saves a project-bound receipt in user-local liftoff/update-previews storage outside the repository; the receipt is not approval. Apply needs the same checkout and receipt store. Noninteractive apply requires --approve-plan; force and JSON are not consent. Production files, history, and provisioning collisions remain protected; force cannot bypass compatibility. Current updates target manifest v8 and bind captured configuration without changing recorded workload, workflow, agents, profile or layout. Pending updates never recover implicitly: use \`liftoff update <project> --recover --approve-plan <saved-fingerprint>\`. Exit 0: clean or approved scope completed; 2: drift or committed migration with incomplete revalidation; 1: rejected or failed operation.

Usage
Usage: liftoff update [project-path]

Arguments
Argument: project-path | Description: Generated project to reconcile

Project options
Option: --project <path> | Description: Project path

Command options
Option: --check | Description: Preview normal and eligible forced plans without project writes; save an external preview receipt

Consent options
Option: --force | Description: Select the separately previewed forced plan for exact owned-core conflicts and retired aliases; still requires approval
Option: --approve-plan <fingerprint> | Description: Approve the exact effective plan from check using its full lowercase 64-hex SHA-256 fingerprint
Option: --recover | Description: Recover only the interrupted update selected by --approve-plan; use the exact project root or an explicit project path

Output options
Option: --json | Description: Emit one schema-4 v8 update result on stdout; interactive approval uses stderr and still defaults to no

General options
Option: --help | Description: Show command-specific help

"
`;

exports[`complete help screens > snapshots plain upgrade command help 1`] = `
"LIFTOFF / UPGRADE - Replace the supported global npm Liftoff CLI; project templates use update separately

Usage
Usage: liftoff upgrade

Command options
Option: --check | Description: Check for an installable stable CLI update without changing anything

Output options
Option: --json | Description: Emit one machine-readable result object

General options
Option: --help | Description: Show command-specific help

"
`;

exports[`complete help screens > snapshots rich adopt command help 1`] = `
"┌─ LIFTOFF / ADOPT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Start with \`liftoff adopt --project <path> --check\`. Bare JSON and non-TTY invocations also  │
│ preview only. Preview records are stored outside the repository and are observations, not    │
│ verification, file approval, transaction ownership, active-binding publication, deployment   │
│ authority, or recovery proof. The target workload, workflow, agents, profile, plugins, and   │
│ layout come from the installed release plus explicit target flags/configuration. Existing    │
│ Liftoff projects use \`liftoff update --check\` and separately authorized \`liftoff repair      │
│ --check\`, never re-adoption. A complete later public plan requires exact \`--approve-plan     │
│ <fingerprint>\`; registration of the flag cannot approve discovery or a blocked compatibility │
│ review. Recovery requires \`--recover --approve-plan <fingerprint>\` and may address only that │
│ authenticated transaction. Bare interactive execution can prompt only after displaying a     │
│ complete current executable plan and defaults to no; blocked or incomplete previews never    │
│ prompt. JSON, piped answers, manifest absence, process age, PID, generic yes, and force are  │
│ not consent. Unresolved mappings, dynamic behavior, missing checks, unsupported conversions, │
│ collisions, existing deployment/state, and unsafe boundaries remain blockers. No commit,     │
│ branch switch, stash/reset, push, database/cloud mutation, starter replacement, or implicit  │
│ telemetry enrollment is authorized. Exit 2: safe preview or existing-project route needs     │
│ further review; 1: invalid/unsafe/unavailable approval or recovery.                          │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
┌─ Usage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ liftoff adopt [project-path]                                                                 │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
┌─ Arguments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Argument      Description                                                                    │
│ ────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ project-path  Supported non-Liftoff Git project or explicitly identified non-Git application │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
┌─ Project options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option                      Description                                                      │
│ ──────────────────────────  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────       │
│ --type <workload>           Project workload type                                            │
│ --genai / --no-genai        Create a GenAI project; use --no-genai for a standard API        │
│ --api <stack>               Backend API stack                                                │
│ --pattern <pattern>         GenAI application pattern                                        │
│ --cloud <provider>          Cloud provider (default: azure)                                  │
│ --region <region>           Cloud deployment region (default: eastus)                        │
│ --frontend / --no-frontend  Include the Vue frontend starter (default: false)                │
│ --environments <list>       Comma-separated environments (default: dev,staging,prod)         │
│ --config <file>             Load deterministic project options from JSON                     │
│ --project <path>            Exact project path; explicitly select non-Git applications       │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
┌─ Framework options ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option                                Description                                            │
│ ────────────────────────────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ --spec <workflow>                     Development workflow: openspec, spec-kit, or manual    │
│                                       (default: openspec)                                    │
│ --agents <list>                       Comma-separated AI coding agents; none is valid only   │
│                                       for Manual (default: copilot; none for Manual)         │
│ --default-agent <agent>               Primary agent for Spec Kit when multiple agents are    │
│                                       selected                                               │
│ --governance <profile>                Repository-governance profile:                         │
│                                       single-maintainer-gitflow, team-gitflow, or none       │
│                                       (default: single-maintainer-gitflow)                   │
│ --copilot-cloud / --no-copilot-cloud  Set up the GitHub-hosted Copilot coding agent for      │
│                                       OpenSpec (default: false)                              │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
┌─ Command options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option   Description                                                                         │
│ ───────  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────                 │
│ --check  Preview only and save bounded review records outside the repository                 │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
┌─ Consent options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option                        Description                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ --approve-plan <fingerprint>  Approve one complete current public adoption plan by its full  │
│                               lowercase 64-hex SHA-256 fingerprint                           │
│ --recover                     Inspect or continue only the authenticated recovery owned by   │
│                               --approve-plan                                                 │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
┌─ Output options ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option  Description                                                                          │
│ ──────  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────               │
│ --json  Emit one schema-1 adoption result on stdout; bare JSON always previews               │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
┌─ General options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option  Description                                                                          │
│ ──────  ──────────────────────────                                                           │
│ --help  Show command-specific help                                                           │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
"
`;

